#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_shift_left

#% text
# `bit_shift_left(k, s)` gives the integer k shifted left by s bits, k 2^s; `bit_shift_left(k)` shifts by one bit.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A negative s shifts right, as `bit_shift_right(k, -s)`. Lists thread over k.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_shift_left(32, 3)
#% output
#= 256

#% cell
bit_shift_left(32)
#% output
#= 64

#% cell
bit_shift_left([1, 2, 4, 16], 2)
#% output
#= [4, 8, 16, 64]

#% cell
bit_shift_left(2^100 - 1, 7) == (2^100 - 1)*2^7
#% output
#= true

#% cell
bit_shift_left(100, -2)
#% output
#= 25

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_shift_right`, `bit_length`
